1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,180
The moon is falling towards the Earth

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:05,360
right now. Every second, it moves sideways

3
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:08,140
about a kilometer and drops a tiny bit

4
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:08,980
towards us.

5
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:12,600
But the Earth curves away beneath it, so

6
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:13,700
it keeps on missing.

7
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:17,100
Isaac Newton worked this out more than

8
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:20,320
three hundred years ago. An orbit isn't

9
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:23,480
floating at all. It's falling and missing

10
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:24,240
forever
